On 10/26/2015 01:50 AM, MorphemeAddict wrote:
> When did it become illegal to have final consonant clusters in names?
>

Never.

> On Sun, Oct 25, 2015 at 1:32 PM, selpahi <seladwa@gmx.de> wrote:
>
>     la .piier. cu cusku di'e
>
>         How would you Lojbanize "Frankfurt"? To me the best option seems
>         to be
>         ".frankyfuryt."
>
>
>     There are two types of cmevla in Lojban: jbocme, which consist only
>     of lojbanic syllables, and zifcme, which are just a string of
>     phonemes that don't violate any phonotactic constraints (e.g.
>     voicing rules, invalid clusters etc) but ignore syllabic structure.
>
>     {.frankfurt.} is a valid zifcme, but not a jbocme, because it
>     contains syllables whose coda contains more than one consonant.
>

Since {.frankfurt.} is a zifcme, and zifcme are a subclass of cmevla, 
there's no problem here.

.i mi'e la tsani mu'o

